      "standardized_narrative": "As at 31 December 2021 gross claims outstanding were $145.318m (up from $124.620m at 1 January 2021). The report does not separately quantify a gross prior-year-only reserve movement; overall reserve levels and claims activity were driven by natural catastrophe events (Hurricane Ida, Storm Uri and various 2020 US hurricanes and 2019 typhoons), increased cyber/ransomware claims and the wider COVID-19 and geopolitical environment. The syndicate writes primarily property reinsurance and cyber business, and these areas were the main drivers of claims volatility in the period.",
